# =============================================================================
# .vercelignore — what does not belong on the internet
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything in this repository that is not the shop. None of it is secret —
# this project has no credentials in source, and a check in
# scripts/check-syntax.mjs fails the build if one ever appears — but "not
# secret" is not the same as "worth publishing".
#
# The rule being applied is the smallest possible public surface. A file that
# nobody needs and that nobody can ask for is a file that cannot be read
# wrongly, cannot be probed, and cannot come up in a search.
#
# WHY EACH ONE
#
#   dev/       A development web server, complete with its own routing. It
#              never runs on Vercel — the platform serves the files and the
#              functions itself — so shipping it would be publishing a second
#              server that happens not to be listening.
#
#   db/        The schema, the policies and the migrations. RLS is the
#              security boundary and it holds whether or not anybody can read
#              the file that declares it, so this is not a hole being closed.
#              It is simply a map of the database with no reason to be handed
#              out at the front door.
#
#   scripts/   The seed, the verification suites and make-admin.mjs. They run
#              on a machine with the service role key in its environment, and
#              that environment is nowhere near a browser. Publishing them
#              tells a reader exactly which administrative commands exist.
#
#   .env.example
#              Committed on purpose and safe by design — every value in it is
#              a placeholder. It is for whoever clones the repository, not for
#              whoever visits the shop.
#
# WHAT IS NOT IGNORED, AND MUST NOT BE
#   index.html, admin/, assets/, data/, api/  — the shop, the panel, and the
#   functions. data/ in particular is still fetched by both documents.
# =============================================================================

dev/
db/
scripts/
.env.example
